    "title": "James Gearhart Obituary - Reading, PA",
    "text": "James V. Gearhart OBITUARY\nJames V. Gearhart OBITUARY\nJames V. “Jim” Gearhart, 80, of Fellowship Community, Whitehall, went to be with his Lord and Savior, Saturday,\nDecember 27, 2025. He was the husband of Carol (Mann) Gearhart to whom he was married 48 years. Born in Harrisburg,\nMay 15, 1945, Jim was the son of the late Vernon and Elinor (Heck) Gearhart. Jim was Valedictorian of his high school\nclass at John Harris High School in Harrisburg and went on to earn his bachelor’s degree in history from Haverford\nCollege. He retired as Chief Budget Officer at Kutztown University after 30 years. Having well rounded interests, he\nenjoyed reading, travel, vacationing at Stone Harbor, NJ, watching sports and photography. Jim was a member of Cedar\nCrest Bible Fellowship Church, Allentown.\nIn addition to his loving wife, Carol, Jim is survived by daughters, Diana J. Blackford and her husband, Ty of Sidney, OH,\nAmy E. Wesner and her husband, Eric of Bethel; grandchildren, Simon, Anderson, and Eva Blackford and Jamie and Paul\nWesner; predeceased by brother, John Gearhart.\nA service to honor and celebrate Jim’s life will be held 11:00 a.m., Saturday, January 3, 2026 at the Zentz Community\nCenter, 3000 Fellowship Drive, Whitehall (on the Fellowship Community Campus), with the Rev. Carl Fischer, Jr.,\nofficiating. The family will receive relatives and friends from 10:00 – 11:00 a.m. Saturday prior to the service. Private\ninterment will be held at Laureldale Cemetery, Reading. The Heintzelman -Stephens Funeral Home, P.C., has been\nentrusted with the arrangements. Online expressions of sympathy may be recorded at www.heintzelmanstephens.com.\nContributions: In lieu of flowers, memorial contributions may be made to the Benevolent Fund at Fellowship Community\nc/o Lisa Hazler 3000 Fellowship Drive, Whitehall PA 18052.",
